<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        Use the <strong>Availability</strong> tab to tell your managers when you can't work, or would rather
        work, each week, for example "college on Tuesday evenings". They see it when they build the rota.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="Adding a time">
        <ol>
            <li>Select <strong>Add a time</strong>.</li>
            <li>Choose whether it's a time you can't work or would rather work, the day, and <strong>All day</strong>
                or a <strong>From</strong> and to time. A time can run past midnight into the next day.</li>
            <li>If it only applies for a while, set <strong>Starting</strong> and <strong>Until</strong> dates.</li>
            <li>Add a note if it helps your manager, and save.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>Use the edit and delete buttons on a time to change or remove it.</FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="How much you'd like to work">
        <FluentText>
            At the top of the tab, under <strong>How much I'd like to work</strong>, fill in
            <strong>At most shifts a week</strong>, <strong>At most hours a week</strong>, or both, and select
            <strong>Save</strong>. Leave a box empty for no limit, or empty both and save to remove it.
        </FluentText>
        <FluentText>
            It's a wish, not a promise: when the rota is built, people who'd go past it are picked after everyone
            who wouldn't. Your contract still sets the most you can be given.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpNote>
        When your manager asks Lanyard to suggest staff for a shift, people who can't work at that time are
        left out of the suggestions. Your manager can still put you on the shift, but they're warned first.
        It isn't a booking, so for a particular day off use <strong>Request time off</strong> instead.
    </HelpNote>
</HelpTab>
